<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuhi V Musinga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1883–<a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Musinga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuhi V Musinga was king of Rwanda from 1896 to 1931. Brought to the throne as a youth by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coup-of-rucunshu">Coup of Rucunshu</a>, he ruled at first under the control of his mother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanjogera">Kanjogera</a> and her kinsmen, and in 1897 accepted German protection. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyanza-rwanda">Nyanza</a> the permanent royal seat. Under Belgian rule he resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and colonial reforms, and in 1931 the Belgians deposed and exiled him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yuhi-v-musinga.jpg" alt="Yuhi V Musinga" width="320" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:YuhiVMusinga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Musinga came to power as a young teenager in a palace coup that overturned the short reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mibambwe-iv-rutarindwa">Mibambwe IV Rutarindwa</a>, the chosen successor of the powerful king Kigeri Rwabugiri. The coup was organised by members of the Bega clan, among them Rwabugiri's widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanjogera">Kanjogera</a>, Musinga's mother. Because kingship was normally conferred by clear ritual protocol, an accession of this kind left his legitimacy in question throughout his reign.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Reign</h2><p>His regime was at first unpopular and earned the nickname Cyiimyamaboko, &quot;It is force that rules&quot;, for its reliance on the forces behind the coup. He leaned on his mother's clan and on the Germans, and faced many revolts. The most serious was the rebellion of Ndungutse in 1912, led by a man who claimed to be a son of Rutarindwa; it won wide support in northern Rwanda and was defeated only after German intervention.</p><p>Many regions occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kigeli-iv-rwabugiri">Rwabugiri</a>'s armies had broken away after his death. German power was used to reassert royal authority over autonomous areas, and court delegates served as colonial administrators, above all under Belgian rule after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. The court also tried to use the White Fathers, the Missionnaires d'Afrique, to extend its legitimacy, but this collaboration split the court into rival factions allied with different outsiders. A major famine struck in 1928–29.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>In November 1931 the Belgian administration deposed Musinga, citing his inability to work with subordinate chiefs and his refusal to be baptised a Roman Catholic, and replaced him with his eldest son, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutara-iii-rudahigwa">Mutara III Rudahigwa</a>. Musinga was exiled first to Kamembe in south-western Rwanda and then to Kilembwe in south-eastern Congo. He died of natural causes on 13 January 1944.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Yuhi V Musinga” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Nyanza became the permanent seat only under <b>Yuhi V Musinga</b> around 1899.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-rwanda">Kingdom of Rwanda · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in the Kingdom of Rwanda. Died in Moba, in what is now <a href="/countries/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">the Democratic Republic of the Congo</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=-7.04,29.78&amp;year=1922" aria-label="Moba on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: the place of death of Yuhi V Musinga"><image href="/maps/globes/g03000.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4981 5601h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4981 5601h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=-7.04,29.78&amp;year=1922">What was here in 1922? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
